          "value": "Japanese models crowd the upper MPG half of the brush—several points push into the forties with a max near 47—while American cars only sprinkle into that band and top out closer to the high thirties. The brushed view therefore reads as a Japan-led efficiency cluster with the US entries sparser and lower on the MPG axis.",
